    </files-touched>

    <transitional-export-note>
      A plain `export * from './WizardFollowOns'` at the components barrel FAILS
      the build (TS2308) because AssignWorkFollowOnStep, CreateEventFollowOnStep,
      WORK_ASSIGNMENT_PRIORITY, FOLLOW_ON_CANONICAL_ORDER, IRecipientItem (+ prop
      types) are STILL exported by CreateRecordWizard during the migration window.
      Per the established codebase convention (SummarizeFilesWizard/index.ts avoids
      duplicate re-exports), components/index.ts re-exports only the genuinely-new
      names (FollowOnGrid, FollowOnCardConfig, FOLLOW_ON_ID_MAP, FOLLOW_ON_LABEL_MAP,
      followOnStepId, SendEmailFollowOnStep, DraftSummaryFollowOnStep,
      AddTodoFollowOnStep, createTodoRegardingChild + types). The duplicated names
      remain importable from the WizardFollowOns barrel directly. Verified via grep
      that NO consumer imports any colliding name from the @spaarke/ui-components
      root, so nothing regresses. ACTION FOR TASK 021 (or whichever deletes the last
      CreateRecordWizard follow-on copy): flip components/index.ts to
      `export * from './WizardFollowOns'`.
    </transitional-export-note>

